{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hand one to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and a denial stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"being a bare 403: the guard mints a fresh permission ticket for the pair the caller lacked and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches it to the thrown ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","type":"reference"},{"text":", so the framework adapter can return it as a header and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a UMA-aware client knows where to go for authority instead of only being told “no”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in, and deliberately so."}]},{"text":" Emitting a challenge means minting a credential — a wire call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the Protection API, and a live ticket, produced on a path the caller did not explicitly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. A guard that did that on every denial by default would turn each unauthorized request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into a Protection API call, which is a denial-of-service amplifier pointed at your own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authorization server. So it happens only where an application asked for it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Failure is not escalation."}]},{"type":"text","text":" If minting fails — the PAT expired, the Protection API is down,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the resource declares none of the requested scopes — the denial still surfaces as an ordinary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" without a challenge. A caller who was going to be refused is refused either way;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"letting a Protection API outage turn a deny into a 503 would hand the outage a second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consequence, and letting it turn into an allow would be a security bug."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A configured "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WWW-Authenticate: UMA"},{"type":"text","text":" challenge emitter (CONTRACT.md §20.3, emit half)."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/init(realm:asURI:pat:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/pat","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/realm"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger"]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UmaChallenger","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13UmaChallengerV","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure"},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/realm":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/realm","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"realm","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"title":"realm","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/realm","abstract":[{"text":"The protection realm named in the header.","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/asURI":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The authorization server the caller should redeem the ticket at — normally this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deployment’s issuer, read from "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/umaDiscover()"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than concatenated by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hand, for the same reason §12.3 rule 6 gives."}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"asURI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/asuri","title":"asURI","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamGuards/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"requireAccess","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resource","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scope","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"umaChallenge","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK13UmaChallengerV"},{"text":"?) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AxiamGuardHandler","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A12GuardHandlera"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamguards\/requireaccess(_:resource:scope:umachallenge:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"require_access(action, resource[, scope])"},{"type":"text","text":" (§11): the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"authenticated caller","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" must pass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an AXIAM authorization check. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subject_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the end user’s id (§11.2 rule 2), not the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"application’s service-account session."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","title":"requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/pat":{"abstract":[{"text":"A Protection API Token: a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"client-credentials","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" token carrying the ","type":"text"},{"code":"uma_protection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" scope","ty